ir deaths are  gonna have any meaning is if the ship  sets sail and they're able to stop the  rumbling if flock and the other jaegers  manage to prevent that then it means  that connie would have killed his  friends for no reason and that's why  he's so determined to make sure his  actions weren't in vain  meanwhile up on the rooftops hanji  notices a train full of reinforcements  heading towards the harbour  on this train are the additional waves  of jaegers that we mentioned earlier and  with the alliance barely holding on as  it is the commander knew they had to  deal with this train as a priority  luckily for them it was blown up out of  nowhere before they had to do anything  and the person responsible was  instructor chadis later in the video  i'll explain exactly why he did this but  for now all we need to know is that he  was inspired to take action after seeing  the scouts working together with annie  speaking of the female titan after  taking one too many thunderspears her  head had now been decapitated not for  the first time while rhino wasn't doing  much better in this state the two  warriors weren't able to move or see  anything respectively making them both  sitting darks as the aegis made a move  to kill them however at the last moment  connie makes a heroic entrance as he  slices down a whole group of enemy  soldiers while mikasa supports him by  taking out the ones who are shooting at  the same time jon chips in by shooting  more jaegers with his rifle and this  moment was brutal because you could tell  the girl he killed was absolutely  terrified  anyway soon after this the card titan  finally joins the battle by breaking  through the rooftop and we get this cool  sequence of her evading about 50  thunderspear attacks  on the ground falco then runs towards  the action having already cut his hand  and this injury serves as the catalyst  for his first ever transformation i  gotta say this shot of his titan  emerging from the lightning was easily  on