mbling if the boat is destroyed  along the way he maneuvers past falco  pushes back hanji and uses one of his  two thunderspears on peak meaning he had  just one final shot to save eldir if he  could accurately fire this thunderspear  then parodies would have been saved  while the rest of the world would be  trampled but as he went to fire gabby  shot him in his other arm which  completely messed up the trajectory  the result was that both flock and his  thunderspear fell into the water and the  yagris had lost the one person who was  keeping them organized from that point  onwards the battle then basically became  a massacre with mikasa brutally  murdering her fellow islanders in the  most imaginative ways she could find  while this was happening onyankpon and  the mechanics had been loading the ship  with coal the entire time and with the  alliance now taking control of the port  the ship was finally ready to leave  there was of course a brief moment at  the end where falco began to lose  control of his titan but generally  speaking this wasn't that strange we saw  with aaron how certain people can go  berserk when using their titans for the  first time and pique vaguely warned  falco that his first transformation  wouldn't go well  thankfully before things could escalate  magus shut up to slice him out of there  and with that the main part of the war  was officially over all that was left  was to tie up some loose ends and this  is why the general stayed behind on the  island while everyone else got on board  the ship  over the years paradise has captured  various warships belonging to the malia  navy and mcgath knew that this cruiser  had the potential to catch up with the  alliance  this was a chance that mcgath  understandably wasn't willing to take so  much so that he was fully prepared to  die so that the rest of the alliance  could maintain their pursuit of eren  now regarding instructor shardis he  swoops in to kill a couple of jaegers  that were pursuing 