n and i think she  was grateful to him for this similar to  how she was grateful to that god who was  killed earlier in the season  moving on to the post-credits scene this  moment happens hours later when annie's  healed from her injuries and she's told  by the commander that they won't be  going to liberia as i mentioned earlier  the female titan wasn't aware that  saving liberia was impossible but after  hearing the news she collapses to her  knees as she's now lost her will to keep  fighting her promise to her dad was the  only thing giving her the motivation to  keep moving on but with that promise now  dead she barely has anything to live for  hanji goes on to explain however that  mcgath didn't sacrifice himself just for  the sake of mali or liberio but rather  it was to save as many unknown innocent  people as they could in that way the  command is trying to convince annie that  stopping the rumbling is a cause worth  fighting for even if her father can't be  saved  in response annie returns to the  original question she asked around the  campfire which is whether mikasa or any  of the scouts are prepared to kill aaron  if they're not prepared for aaron to die  then it will lead to a civil war between  both sides of the alliance and  considering where annie is mentally  right now she doesn't have the  conviction to fight with them or even  fight with aaron himself  the episode then ends with an aerial  shot of the ship as it makes his way  towards the hangar and the question of  whether the scouts are prepared to kill  aaron still remains unanswered  anyway people that was my breakdown for  episode 27 of attack on titan season 4  and remember the season finale won't be  coming out until the 3rd of april be  sure to sub so you don't miss my review  of that final episode and i'll also be  doing an update video if they announce a  part 3 for the final season  until the next one peace out
 

